    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0788" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg692"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woodford to the
                            President.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>My No. 45. Unless report on the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>
                    requires immediate action, I suggest that nothing be decided or done until after
                    the receipt of my personal letters 43, 44, and 46, which my second secretary of
                    legation will carry from Gibraltar Monday, March 21. I also suggest that you
                    authorize me to tell the Queen informally, or any minister indicated by her,
                    that you wish final agreement before April 15. If you will acquaint me fully
                    with general settlement desired I believe Spanish Government will offer without
                    compulsion and upon its own motion such terms of settlement as may be
                    satisfactory to both nations. Large liberty as to details should be conceded to
                    Spain, but your friendship is recognized and appreciated, and I now believe it
                    will be a pleasure to Spanish Government to propose what will probably be
                    satisfactory to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodford.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
